So nutzt du generierte API:

```ts
import { Api } from '@/sdk/generated/Api';
import type { ListProjectsData } from '@/sdk/generated/data-contracts';

const api = new Api<{ token: string }>({
  baseUrl: 'http://localhost:3000',
  securityWorker: (securityData) => {
    if (!securityData?.token) return {};

    return {
      headers: {
        Authorization: `Bearer ${securityData.token}`,
      },
    };
  },
});

api.setSecurityData({ token: 'DEIN_BEARER_TOKEN' });
```

Dann Calls:

```ts
const projectsRes = await api.listProjects();
const projects: ListProjectsData = projectsRes.data;
console.log(projects);

const appRes = await api.getApp({ id: 'app-id' });
console.log(appRes.data);

const appsRes = await api.listApps({ projectId: 'project-id' });
console.log(appsRes.data);
```

Wichtig:
- `baseUrl` nur Host. Nicht `/api/v1`, weil Pfade in SDK schon `/api/v1/...` enthalten.
- Ergebnis liegt in `.data`
- Fehler werfen Exception via `throw data`

Create/Update Beispiel:

```ts
const created = await api.saveProject({
  name: 'My Project',
  projectType: 'APP',
});

console.log(created.data.id);
```

Mit Try/Catch:

```ts
try {
  const res = await api.deleteApp({ id: 'app-id' });
  console.log(res.data);
} catch (err) {
  console.error(err);
}
```

Wenn du kein `securityWorker` willst:

```ts
const api = new Api({
  baseUrl: 'http://localhost:3000',
});

const res = await api.listProjects({
  headers: {
    Authorization: 'Bearer DEIN_TOKEN',
  },
});
```

Node-Script komplett:

```ts
import { Api } from './src/generated/Api';

async function main() {
  const api = new Api<{ token: string }>({
    baseUrl: 'http://localhost:3000',
    securityWorker: (securityData) => ({
      headers: securityData?.token
        ? { Authorization: `Bearer ${securityData.token}` }
        : {},
    }),
  });

  api.setSecurityData({ token: process.env.QUICKSTACK_TOKEN! });

  const projects = await api.listProjects();
  console.log(projects.data);
}

main().catch(console.error);
```

Warum `api.listProjects()`?
- Methoden liegen direkt auf der generierten `Api`-Klasse.

Typen aus OpenAPI nutzen:
```ts
import type { SaveProjectPayload, SaveProjectData } from './src/generated/data-contracts';

const payload: SaveProjectPayload = {
  name: 'My Project',
  projectType: 'APP',
};

const created = await api.saveProject(payload);
const project: SaveProjectData = created.data;
```

Wenn du willst, baue ich dir jetzt kleine Wrapper-Datei wie `src/sdk/quickstack-client.ts`, damit du nur noch `quickstack.listProjects()` schreibst.


